<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( Unit testing serves as the foundation of our quality assurance strategy, ensuring that individual components behave as expected in isolation. This includes utility functions, API route handlers, and frontend UI elements. By validating logic at the smallest testable level, we reduce the risk of regressions, simplify debugging, and accelerate development cycles. Unit tests also act as living documentation, clarifying the intended behavior of each module for future contributors.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Tools)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (We use Jest as the primary testing framework for both backend and frontend logic. On the backend, Jest handles validation of Express route handlers, PostgreSQL-triggered logic, and game lifecycle utilities. On the frontend, Jest is paired with React Testing Library to test component rendering, state transitions, and user interactions. All test suites are structured to run independently, with mocking strategies applied to isolate dependencies such as database calls, socket events, and external APIs.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
